The xLSTM architecture introduces several significant innovations that address the limitations of classical LSTM. First, it implements an improved gating mechanism for enhanced memory management through scalar LSTM (sLSTM). This mechanism replaces the standard sigmoid function in the input and forget gates with an exponential activation function. To mitigate potential numerical instability from large exponential values, the model stabilizes gates with an additional state \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
