For structural feature extraction, we implemented a GNN approach to model the two-dimensional molecular topology. The peptide sequences were first converted to SMILES, which were subsequently transformed into molecular graph representations using RDKit (version 2025.09.01). The node and edge features provide a rich representation of the peptide chemical structure. The graph feature extraction network was composed of three message passing layers, a global readout layer, and an average pooling layer. The output extracted graph feature has a dimension of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
