Among the evaluated specialized DL frameworks, AOPP consistently outperformed AnOxPePred across all three benchmark datasets. This performance gain can be attributed to its capability of Bi-LSTM architectures to capture bidirectional sequential dependencies in peptide sequences compared to the conventional CNNs. Compared to the next best DL method AOPP, our proposed Multi-AOP framework achieved further improvements in classification accuracies, reaching 0.8043 (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
